      "message": "Could the body say what goes wrong without this patch? As far as I can see, a 4KB process gets `-EIO` when it maps one 4KB page of the status file, and a 16KB mapping at offset 4KB reads the first 4KB of the page after the status page (see the inline comment). The second one is worth stating, since it exposes kernel memory.\n\nFor the policy, it could say that a 4KB process reads zeroes past the end of the policy, up to the next 16KB boundary, instead of getting `SIGBUS`. The new fault check looks right to me.",
