      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T22:33:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that this check needs fixing: today a 4KB process can map 16KB at offset 4KB, which gives `vm_pgoff \u003d\u003d 0` and `vm_slice_off \u003d\u003d 1`, so it passes. Since aosp/4368055, `remap_pfn_range()` then maps slices 1 to 3 of the status page and the first 4KB of the page after it. The `vma_file_offset()` check closes that, thanks.\n\nI\u0027m worried `vma_page_size()` reverts `983c0ad4d20e` (`\"ANDROID: 16K: Fix selinux mmap size check\"`) on x86_64 with page size emulation, though: there `__PAGE_SIZE` is the emulated 16KB and every VMA is a multiple of it, while `vma_page_size()` is the 4KB kernel page, so the status mmap would fail with `-EIO` again.\n\nCould the 4KB size apply only to 4KB VMAs, as for perf on aosp/4367963, keeping the original comment? Something like:\n\n```\n\t/* only allows one page from the head */\n\tif (vma_file_offset(vma) ||\n\t    size !\u003d (vma_is_p3s_4k(vma) ? vma_page_size(vma) : __PAGE_SIZE))\n\t\treturn -EIO;\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "47d3e4bc218b285b3320bb60a4d7ca74b7899500",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
